As an AI language model, I cannot write PHP, but I can provide you with a general structure and logic of a newsfeed in PHP.

Structure of Newsfeed in PHP:

1. Database: You need to create a database that stores the information related to news such as title, description, author, date, image, etc.

2. Connection: Establish a connection to the database with PHP MySQLi or PDO.

3. Query: Execute a query to fetch all the news from the database.

4. Loop: Use a loop in PHP to iterate through all the news and display them on the web page.

5. HTML: Use HTML to structure the news in a well-organized way. You can use CSS to apply styles to HTML elements.

Example Code:

```
<?php
// Establish a connection to the database
$servername = "localhost";
$username = "username";
$password = "password";
$dbname = "newsfeed";

$conn = mysqli_connect($servername, $username, $password, $dbname);

if (!$conn) {
    die("Connection failed: " . mysqli_connect_error());
}

// Execute a query to fetch all the news from the database
$sql = "SELECT * FROM news ORDER BY id DESC";
$result = mysqli_query($conn, $sql);

// Use a loop to iterate through all the news and display them on the web page
while($row = mysqli_fetch_assoc($result)) {
    echo "<div class='news'>";
    echo "<img src='".$row['image']."'>";
    echo "<h2>".$row['title']."</h2>";
    echo "<p>".$row['description']."</p>";
    echo "<span>Author: ".$row['author']."</span>";
    echo "<span>Date: ".$row['date']."</span>";
    echo "</div>";
}

// Close the database connection
mysqli_close($conn);
?>
```

